; coverage for set.kurt's "power-set" axiom (`Pow($a) = { $b | $b ⊂ $a }`) -- never exercised by
; any proof file before this one, unlike `∩`/`∪`/`⊂` which are worked in
; proofs/mafi1/001-two-equal-sets.kurt already.
load set
const A

; every set is a subset of itself, so every set is a member of its own power set -- shown by
; unfolding "power-set" via "set-comprehension" (kurt's single-hop derivation can't chain
; "power-set" and "set-comprehension" through the literal `Pow(A)` notation in one step, so
; both facts are stated explicitly rather than concluding with `A ∈ Pow(A)` directly)
show A ⊂ A
proof
    let x
        x ∈ A implies x ∈ A
    A ⊂ A
qed
A ∈ { $b | $b ⊂ A }  ≡  A ⊂ A
Pow(A) = { $b | $b ⊂ A }

; the empty-set case: originally dropped from this file entirely, since it needs unfolding
; `∅`'s own definition (`def ∅ = { $a | false }`) and matching a comprehension body that's
; *exactly* `false` -- zero occurrences of the comprehension's own bound variable -- which
; "set-comprehension" couldn't match at all before the `generate_all_combinations` fix (see
; doc/kurt-soundness.md #6). Two explicit hops, same reasoning as above (`Pow(A)`'s own
; unfolding is a separate hop from "set-comprehension"):
const y
y ∈ { $a | false }  ≡  false             ; the real regression coverage for the fix itself
∅ = { $a | false }                       ; restating "empty set" 's own definition
y ∈ ∅  ≡  false
